  "assumptions": [
    "All five columns are forecasts: N=2027; N+1=2028; N+2=2029; N+3=2030; N+4=2031. The template Actual (if applicable) caption is not a claim of actual 2027 data.",
    "Company management reports EUR300000 cash and no outstanding debt or short-term liabilities on3November2026. Carrying EUR300000 into1January2027 is an explicit forecast assumption, requiring the intervening burn bridge. The source opening cash and legacy debt/accrual are reconciled through opening forecast net assets, not a new cash contribution or debt forgiveness.",
    "The old forecast legacy principal EUR250000 and opening accrued interest EUR10208.33 are removed. This removes EUR250000 financing repayment and EUR13125 operating interest settlement in2027, while removing only EUR2916.67 current-year interest expense. The opening equity adjustment identifies those balances and the opening-cash change explicitly. Future term-debt draws remain conditional forecasts.",
    "Unconverted subscription instruments are presented within other forecast equity, without assigning a BSA-AIR conversion percentage or a future legal share allocation. The saved model balance is a bookkeeping projection; the current instrument ledger and next-round terms determine actual legal economics.",
    "Saved company operating revenue and baseline source costs are retained. This conservative scenario adds the complete EIC qualification and commercial launch programme to baseline costs; no automatic absorption or operating saving is assumed. Reconcile baseline allocations before final management adoption to remove any proven duplicate, not by treating new work as free.",
